# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLIENT env (VITE_*) — these are PUBLIC: Vite inlines them into the browser
# bundle. NEVER put a secret/API key here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Lead form submission endpoint (Formspree form URL, webhook, or your API).
# Used as the direct/fallback target. Example (Formspree): https://formspree.io/f/xxxxxxxx
VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT=

# Cloudflare Turnstile PUBLIC site key. Optional — leave blank to disable bot
# verification (the form then uses VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT directly). When set, the
# form submits through the same-origin /api/lead proxy which verifies the token.
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVER env — set these in Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables (NOT here,
# and NOT prefixed with VITE_ so they stay off the client). Listed for reference.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   LEAD_ENDPOINT         — server-side forward target for /api/lead
#   TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY  — Cloudflare Turnstile secret (enables verification)
#   GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY — enables live Google reviews via /api/reviews
#   GOOGLE_PLACE_ID       — paired with the key above
